%SIXMD 1
# @?INIT - START AND RESPAWN SYSTEM SERVICES

## @?OPTIONS

## @?OPERANDS

## DESCRIPTION

INIT IS THE FIRST USER PROCESS.  IT APPLIES FILESYSTEM MOUNT POLICY FROM
/CONFIG/FSTAB, READS /CONFIG/INITTAB, STARTS THE CONFIGURED SERVICES, WAITS
FOR CHILDREN, AND RESPAWNS ENTRIES MARKED FOR RESPAWN.

INIT MUST RUN AS PROCESS 1.

## @?FILES

### @?/CONFIG/FSTAB
FILESYSTEM MOUNT TABLE READ AT STARTUP.

FSTAB V1 ACCEPTS BLANK LINES, COMMENTS BEGINNING WITH #, AND MEMFS ENTRIES:

MEMFS:/EXISTING/MOUNT/POINT:WORDS

MEMFS IS A SINGLETON.  THE TARGET DIRECTORY MUST ALREADY EXIST.  WORDS IS THE
TOTAL NUMBER OF PDP-10 WORDS RESERVED FOR MEMFS, INCLUDING ITS NODE TABLE.

INIT EXPECTS /TEMP TO BE BACKED BY MEMFS AFTER MOUNTALL COMPLETES.  IF FSTAB
DOES NOT MOUNT MEMFS ON /TEMP, INIT PRINTS A WARNING AND CONTINUES BOOTING.
THIS IS INTENTIONAL ON THE 32K LOW-MEMORY PROFILE, WHICH LEAVES MEMFS
UNMOUNTED TO PRESERVE CORE.

### @?/CONFIG/INITTAB
SYSTEM SERVICE TABLE READ AT STARTUP.

## @?EXIT STATUS

### @?1 - STARTUP FAILED
INIT EXITS ONLY WHEN IT CANNOT RUN AS PROCESS 1 OR CANNOT LOAD ITS REQUIRED
STARTUP CONFIGURATION.
